The gate 'two independent hosts -> identical binary sha256' is measured,
not asserted (D-O1-1): tools/repro_check.py builds the release binary aurad
twice into two independent CARGO_TARGET_DIRs with SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH pinned
to the commit date and path remapping (source root AND per-host target dir —
tonic/prost OUT_DIR includes must not leak either path into panic
locations), and records the identical digests in release/repro.txt. Named
control: repro_mismatch_refused (error: release: repro mismatch: aura-bin,
exit 65); 6/6 mutation NC red (tools/nc_o1.py); 10/10 golden scenarios +
count guard (independent Python-hashlib oracle tools/gen_o1_vectors.py ->
tests/o1_release.rs) against aura_testkit::release (std-only SHA-256,
D-O1-5).

The release process is a checked pipeline (D-O1-2): aura-release check
validates the strict release/manifest.txt against the workspace — semver +
version drift, the '## [0.1.0' CHANGELOG entry, artifact presence,
SHA256SUMS digests, 64-byte detached ed25519 signature structure with the
pinned keyid (D-O1-3; RFC 8032 verify is the wired tools/sign_release.py
step, H1 demo key), the deterministic SBOM regeneration (D-O1-4), the
two-host repro record, and the Dockerfile policy (multi-stage,
digest-pinned bases). aura-release sync regenerates manifest/SHA256SUMS/
SBOM; make repro-check / release-demo / release-check wire the live gate.

Also: docs/evidence/o0 regenerated after fixing the named-control string
check in tools/write_o0_evidence.py (it matched the pre-redesign 'shard 07'
text and reported a false FAIL); the O0 verdicts are unchanged (11/11, 6/6,
live registry=ok shards=10 targets=128).
